g":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H2768","lemma":"חֶרְמוֹן","tr":"cher·mon","gloss":"(Mount) Hermon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H0520","lemma":"אַמָּה","tr":"am·mah","gloss":"cubit","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":247},{"base":"H5511","lemma":"סִיחוֹן","tr":"si·chon","gloss":"Sihon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":37},{"base":"H2809","lemma":"חֶשְׁבּוֹן","tr":"chesh·bon","gloss":"Heshbon","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"DEU","chapter":2,"verse":34,"verseEnd":34,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"At that time we captured all his cities and devoted to destruction the people of every city, including women and children. We left no survivors.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":14,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"In the fourteenth year, Chedorlaomer and the kings allied with him went out and defeated the Rephaites in Ashteroth-karnaim, the Zuzites in Ham, the Emites in Shaveh-kiriathaim,","from":11},{"book":"1KI","chapter":4,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Ben-geber in Ramoth-gilead (the villages of Jair son of Manasseh in Gilead belonged to him, as well as the region of Argob in Bashan with its sixty great cities with walls and bronze bars);","from":4},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Now the people of the half-tribe of Manasseh were numerous. They settled in the land from Bashan to Baal-hermon (that is, Senir, also known as Mount Hermon).","from":9},{"book":"PSA","chapter":29,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"He makes Lebanon skip like a calf, and Sirion like a young wild ox.","from":9},{"book":"LEV","chapter":27,"verse":28,"verseEnd":29,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Nothing that a man sets apart to the LORD from all he owns—whether a man, an animal, or his inherited land—can be sold or redeemed; everything so devoted is most holy to the LORD. No person set apart for destruction may be ransomed; he must surely be put to death.","from":6},{"book":"NUM","chapter":13,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Nevertheless, the people living in the land are strong, and the cities are large and fortified. We even saw the descendants of Anak there.","from":5},{"book":"NUM","chapter":14,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Only do not rebel against the LORD, and do not be afraid of the people of the land, for they will be like bread for us. Their protection has been removed, and the LORD is with us. Do not be afraid of them!”","from":2}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-22":{"people":[{"id":"reuben-h7205","name":"Reuben","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":2,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"og-h5747","name":"Og","kind":"person","brief":"King of Bashan","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"rephaim-h7497b","name":"Rephaim","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"jair-h2971g","name":"Jair","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Segub","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"machir-h4353g","name":"Machir","kind":"person","brief":"Manasseh's son","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":18},{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":21}],"places":[{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":4,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"arnon-h0769","name":"Arnon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"aroer-h6177h","name":"Aroer","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"argob-h0709g","name":"Argob","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"bashan-h1316","name":"Bashan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"geshur-h1650","name":"Geshur","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"havvoth-jair-h2334","name":"Havvoth-jair","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"maacah-h4601r","name":"Maacah","kind":"place","brief":"Near Geshur","count":1,"firstVerse":14},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"jabbok-h2999","name":"Jabbok","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"arabah-h6160g","name":"Arabah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"chinnereth-h3672g","name":"Chinnereth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"pisgah-h6449","name":"Pisgah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"salt-sea-h4417g","name":"Salt Sea","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"words":[{"base":"H9036","lemma":"כֶם","tr":"khem","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":591},{"base":"H1568","lemma":"גִּלְעָד","tr":"gil·ad","gloss":"Gilead","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":134},{"base":"H5158","lemma":"נַ֫חַל","tr":"na·chal","gloss":"torrent: river","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":141},{"base":"H1366","lemma":"גְּבוּל","tr":"ge·vul","gloss":"border: boundary","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":240},{"base":"H1316","lemma":"בָּשָׁן","tr":"ba·shan","gloss":"Bashan","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":60},{"base":"H0709","lemma":"אַרְגֹּב","tr":"ar·gov","gloss":"Argob","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":5},{"base":"H2334","lemma":"חַוּוֹת יָעִיר","tr":"chau·vot ya·ir","gloss":"Havvoth-jair","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":231},{"base":"H1425","lemma":"גָּדִי","tr":"ga·di","gloss":"Gad","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H7206","lemma":"רְאוּבֵנִי","tr":"re·u·ve·ni","gloss":"Reubenite","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":18}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":14,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will fight for you; you need only to be still.”","from":22},{"book":"DEU","chapter":20,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"For the LORD your God goes with you to fight for you against your enemies, to give you the victory.”","from":22},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"The LORD your God, who goes before you, will fight for you, just as you saw Him do for you in Egypt","from":22},{"book":"JOS","chapter":10,"verse":42,"verseEnd":42,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And because the LORD, the God of Israel, fought for Israel, Joshua captured all these kings and their land in one campaign.","from":22},{"book":"2CH","chapter":20,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"You need not fight this battle. Take up your positions, stand firm, and see the salvation of the LORD on your behalf, O Judah and Jerusalem. Do not be afraid or discouraged. Go out and face them tomorrow, for the LORD is with you.’”","from":22},{"book":"2CH","chapter":20,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And the fear of God came upon all the kingdoms of the lands when they heard that the LORD had fought against the enemies of Israel.","from":22},{"book":"ISA","chapter":43,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"But now this is what the LORD says— He who created you, O Jacob, and He who formed you, O Israel: “Do not fear, for I have redeemed you; I have called you by your name; you are Mine!","from":22},{"book":"ISA","chapter":43,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"When you pass through the waters, I will be with you; and when you go through the rivers, they will not overwhelm you. When you walk through the fire, you will not be scorched; the flames will not set you ablaze.","from":22}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"23-29":{"people":[{"id":"joshua-h3091g","name":"Joshua","kind":"person","brief":"A judge","count":1,"firstVerse":28}],"places":[{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"lebanon-h3844g","name":"Lebanon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"pisgah-h6449","name":"Pisgah","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"beth-peor-h1047","name":"Beth-peor","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":29}],"words":[{"base":"H5674","lemma":"עָבַר","tr":"a·var","gloss":"to pass","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":556},{"base":"H1047","lemma":"בֵּית פְּעוֹר","tr":"bet pe·or","gloss":"Beth-peor","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H2088","lemma":"זֶה","tr":"zeh","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":1176},{"base":"H3383","lemma":"יַרְדֵּן","tr":"yar·den","gloss":"Jordan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":182},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":538},{"base":"H6449","lemma":"פִּסְגָּה","tr":"pis·gah","gloss":"Pisgah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1433","lemma":"גֹּ֫דֶל","tr":"go·del","gloss":"greatness","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H5869","lemma":"עַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"eye","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":887},{"base":"H8486","lemma":"תֵּימָן","tr":"te·man","gloss":"south","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H4136","lemma":"מוּל","tr":"mul","gloss":"opposite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Who among the gods is like You, O LORD? Who is like You—majestic in holiness, revered with praises, performing wonders?","from":24},{"book":"DEU","chapter":11,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Know this day that it is not your children who have known and seen the discipline of the LORD your God: His greatness, His mighty hand, and His outstretched arm;","from":24},{"book":"PSA","chapter":71,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Your righteousness reaches to the heavens, O God, You who have done great things. Who, O God, is like You?","from":24},{"book":"DEU","chapter":1,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"The LORD was also angry with me on your account, and He said, “Not even you shall enter the land.","from":26},{"book":"2SA","chapter":7,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"How great You are, O Lord GOD! For there is none like You, and there is no God but You, according to everything we have heard with our own ears.","from":24},{"book":"PSA","chapter":86,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"O Lord, there is none like You among the gods, nor any works like Yours.","from":24},{"book":"JER","chapter":32,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"You show loving devotion to thousands but lay the iniquity of the fathers into the laps of their children after them, O great and mighty God whose name is the LORD of Hosts,","from":24},{"book":"JER","chapter":32,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"openbible","text":"You brought Your people Israel out of the land of Egypt with signs and wonders, with a strong hand and an outstretched arm, and with great terror.","from":24}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}